; This directory's golden-diff rules, aggregated back onto `runtest` (gh-ocannl-726). Each of them
; attaches to its own `runtest-<name>` alias and to NOTHING else, so that `dune build
; @test/operations/runtest-verdict_ratchet` runs that one test and applies its diff; this stanza is
; what keeps `dune runtest` running all of them. Attaching such a rule to `runtest` as well would
; defeat the point: a rule on two aliases makes building either alias build both, so a per-test
; alias that also named `runtest` would pull the whole directory in behind it -- and where the name
; is one dune generates for a `(test)` stanza, dune rejects the pair outright as a dependency cycle.
; Hence the naming: `<name>` is the golden the rule checks, and never a `(test)` stanza's name in
; this directory. A `runtest-<name>` rule missing from this list is one plain `dune runtest` skips
; silently, which `test/operations/env_var_deps` checks -- the same check it makes of the `slow`
