(rule
 ; ocannl-backend: none -- links no backend: it parses every repository OCaml source.
 ; The three file lists are written by dune's own `echo`, which spawns nothing and so has no length
 ; limit, and handed over as `@<path>` response files -- expanded into argv, a repository-wide list
 ; outgrows Windows' 32,767-character command line, where `CreateProcess` fails with `No such file
 ; or directory` and names neither. One file per GROUP, because the groups are what the scan's own
 ; flags separate: a response file splices in where it stood, so `--sources @<list>` reaches the
 ; program as the expanded `--sources a b c` did. See `test/support/scan_argv.ml`.
