; Interfaces built to break the emitter derivation: a library whose .mli declares every shape
; `Emitter_frontier` has to answer for, beside the near misses that decide the rule. Its second
; module carries no .mli and no annotation, which is `C_syntax.compile_proc`'s situation -- the
; member that makes the derivation read compiled interfaces rather than sources -- and having two
; modules is also what makes dune wrap the library, so its interface carries the module aliases the
; derivation takes its module list from.

(library
 (name emitter_fixture)
 (package neural_nets_lib)
 (modules emitter_fixture_a emitter_fixture_b)
 (libraries pprint))

