; How the claim-shape reader behind verdict_ratchet reads a format and a source, on input built to
; break it rather than on whatever the test directories happen to contain today. Also where the
; literals that ratchet plants its canaries on live.

; How the directory reader behind cache_dir_ignores resolves a name, on snippets built to break it.
; The census over the tree exercises only the spellings some source uses today; these pin the rest,
; including the module alias bound in expression position that no source spells yet.

; The benchmark runners' JSON result line, on the values a happy-path run never produces: a
; diverged loss trajectory, times that were never measured, a diagnostic full of control
; characters. Yojson is the parse oracle -- it rejects OCaml's `nan`/`inf` spellings, which is the
; regression (gh-ocannl-676), and the test's last verdicts show that it does.

(test
 ; ocannl-backend: none -- links no backend: it formats and re-parses JSON strings.
 (name bench_result_line)
 (package neural_nets_lib)
 (deps ocannl_config)
 (modules bench_result_line)
 (libraries base stdio yojson bench_json arrayjit.verdict))

